WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.166 --> 00:00:03.190
(swooshing)

00:00:03.190 --> 00:00:05.213
- Hello Believe nation,
I'm Evan Carmichael,

00:00:05.213 --> 00:00:07.931
my one word is believe and
I believe that entrepreneurs

00:00:07.931 --> 00:00:10.449
will solve all the major
problems of the world.

00:00:10.449 --> 00:00:11.843
And so to help you on your journey today,

00:00:11.843 --> 00:00:14.602
I'm going to talk about
the seven must-watch

00:00:14.602 --> 00:00:16.867
TV shows for entrepreneurs.

00:00:16.867 --> 00:00:19.367
♫ Nine, eight

00:00:20.244 --> 00:00:22.827
(techno music)

00:00:25.157 --> 00:00:27.740
(hip hop beat)

00:00:28.682 --> 00:00:30.273
Number one for me is The Profit.

00:00:30.273 --> 00:00:33.080
It's a show put on by
CNBC with Marcus Lemonis.

00:00:33.080 --> 00:00:35.719
Marcus is an angel investor and he goes in

00:00:35.719 --> 00:00:38.390
and he invests his own money
into failing businesses

00:00:38.390 --> 00:00:40.423
and tries to turn them around.

00:00:40.423 --> 00:00:43.037
It's part entertainment and part education

00:00:43.037 --> 00:00:45.241
and he also breaks things down in really

00:00:45.241 --> 00:00:47.973
easy to understand ways
so that even if you're

00:00:47.973 --> 00:00:49.540
just getting started as an entrepreneur,

00:00:49.540 --> 00:00:52.245
or you may not have a
total comprehension of

00:00:52.245 --> 00:00:54.857
finances and balance sheets
and income statements

00:00:54.857 --> 00:00:57.624
and all that stuff, he makes
it easy for you to understand

00:00:57.624 --> 00:01:00.594
and so it's a must-watch,
number one most important one

00:01:00.594 --> 00:01:02.635
that I think entrepreneurs
need to pay attention to.

00:01:02.635 --> 00:01:05.218
(hip hop beat)

00:01:06.065 --> 00:01:07.758
Number two for me is Silicon Valley.

00:01:07.758 --> 00:01:09.895
This is more of a comedy show.

00:01:09.895 --> 00:01:11.631
It's loosely based around things

00:01:11.631 --> 00:01:13.389
that happen in Silicon Valley.

00:01:13.389 --> 00:01:15.531
It's meant as a spoof on the businesses

00:01:15.531 --> 00:01:16.881
and the entrepreneurs and the investors

00:01:16.881 --> 00:01:19.343
that are all down there kind of
in their own different world.

00:01:19.343 --> 00:01:22.137
It's extra funny for
me because I used to be

00:01:22.137 --> 00:01:23.433
a venture capitalist and so I come

00:01:23.433 --> 00:01:26.048
from that world a little
bit and understand it.

00:01:26.048 --> 00:01:29.780
I think if you are not
from the world as much or

00:01:29.780 --> 00:01:31.528
you might be English as a second language

00:01:31.528 --> 00:01:33.185
or you may not have the context,

00:01:33.185 --> 00:01:34.637
it may not be a great show for you.

00:01:34.637 --> 00:01:36.573
Nina, as an example,
doesn't like the show,

00:01:36.573 --> 00:01:39.796
so I have to watch it by myself. Sadness.

00:01:39.796 --> 00:01:41.690
But if you want to
learn a little bit about

00:01:41.690 --> 00:01:43.208
the venture capital
community and have some fun

00:01:43.208 --> 00:01:46.087
laughing at it, Silicon
Valley is worth checking out.

00:01:46.087 --> 00:01:48.670
(hip hop beat)

00:01:49.571 --> 00:01:52.066
Number three is Billions,
this is a pretty new show

00:01:52.066 --> 00:01:54.045
that came out, I think they're
in Season Two right now.

00:01:54.045 --> 00:01:55.210
I love watching this show.

00:01:55.210 --> 00:01:57.675
It's another one where Nina
won't watch it with me.

00:01:57.675 --> 00:02:00.168
I think some of the language
can be really fast as well

00:02:00.168 --> 00:02:02.731
and hard to keep up with
and if you don't really know

00:02:02.731 --> 00:02:05.141
the stock market and how
the rules kind of work

00:02:05.141 --> 00:02:07.741
and the players there, it may
not be interesting for you,

00:02:07.741 --> 00:02:09.720
but it's basically about
this guy who's a billionaire

00:02:09.720 --> 00:02:12.503
who manipulates stock
markets to his own benefit

00:02:12.503 --> 00:02:14.629
and this district attorney
who's always trying to

00:02:14.629 --> 00:02:16.929
catch him and beat him
and send him to jail

00:02:16.929 --> 00:02:18.834
and the fights that they go through,

00:02:18.834 --> 00:02:20.929
webs they try to leave for each other

00:02:20.929 --> 00:02:22.769
and traps that they put each other into.

00:02:22.769 --> 00:02:23.932
I really like this show,

00:02:23.932 --> 00:02:25.224
and I think it's worth checking out.

00:02:25.224 --> 00:02:27.807
(hip hop beat)

00:02:28.916 --> 00:02:30.646
- Dude, we totally hacked in!

00:02:30.646 --> 00:02:32.736
Alright, go now before Evan finds out.

00:02:32.736 --> 00:02:35.612
Hey guys, it's Marcus here
from Affiliate Marketing Dude.

00:02:35.612 --> 00:02:39.476
And today I'm bringing you
the fourth best show on TV

00:02:39.476 --> 00:02:41.865
to watch if you are an entrepreneur.

00:02:41.865 --> 00:02:43.601
And as you could tell by now I've hacked

00:02:43.601 --> 00:02:46.802
into this presentation
to show you Mr. Robot.

00:02:46.802 --> 00:02:49.264
Mr. Robot is a great show that talks about

00:02:49.264 --> 00:02:52.099
entrepreneurship, life, mental issues

00:02:52.099 --> 00:02:54.095
and all kinds of things like that.

00:02:54.095 --> 00:02:56.473
And the reason I chose
it, first and foremost,

00:02:56.473 --> 00:02:59.939
is because of the mental struggle
that Elliot goes through.

00:02:59.939 --> 00:03:02.297
He's a guy, he's a computer
hacker and he's going through

00:03:02.297 --> 00:03:05.745
this mental struggle constantly
to get the things done

00:03:05.745 --> 00:03:07.162
that he wants to do.

00:03:07.162 --> 00:03:08.803
And one of the quotes that I like

00:03:08.803 --> 00:03:12.402
from this very quotable
show is by Elliot himself.

00:03:12.402 --> 00:03:15.353
He says, "Sometimes I
dream of saving the world.

00:03:15.353 --> 00:03:17.673
Saving everybody from the invisible hand,

00:03:17.673 --> 00:03:20.426
the one that brands us
with an employee badge.

00:03:20.426 --> 00:03:23.319
The one that forces us to work for them.

00:03:23.319 --> 00:03:27.404
The one that controls us every
day without us knowing it.

00:03:27.404 --> 00:03:30.583
But I can't stop it. I'm not that special.

00:03:30.583 --> 00:03:32.903
I'm anonymous. I'm just alone."

00:03:32.903 --> 00:03:36.114
Now this is a struggle that
entrepreneurs have all the time.

00:03:36.114 --> 00:03:39.361
Feeling like what they do isn't
going to make a difference.

00:03:39.361 --> 00:03:41.511
But one of the quotes
I have on my desk here

00:03:41.511 --> 00:03:45.240
in my office is something I
came up with years ago that says

00:03:45.240 --> 00:03:47.917
"From this desk I can reach the world".

00:03:47.917 --> 00:03:50.188
And in today's day and
age with technology,

00:03:50.188 --> 00:03:52.430
as an entrepreneur most of the struggle

00:03:52.430 --> 00:03:55.028
you are going to have is a mental struggle

00:03:55.028 --> 00:03:57.364
whether you do something
or don't do something.

00:03:57.364 --> 00:03:59.356
And it's the struggle of decisions.

00:03:59.356 --> 00:04:03.285
And this show is ripe
with examples of deciding

00:04:03.285 --> 00:04:07.046
and the mental struggle and
how businesses can go bad

00:04:07.046 --> 00:04:10.062
and how businesses can go
good and what you can do

00:04:10.062 --> 00:04:12.745
as an individual to make a difference.

00:04:12.745 --> 00:04:15.620
Another quote that I like
from Mr. Robot talks about

00:04:15.620 --> 00:04:18.101
the life of hacking and
how a computer works.

00:04:18.101 --> 00:04:21.170
This also goes into the
mindset of the entrepreneur.

00:04:21.170 --> 00:04:22.897
The quote is, "There's a saying,

00:04:22.897 --> 00:04:24.817
'The devil is at his strongest when we're

00:04:24.817 --> 00:04:25.786
looking the other way.'

00:04:25.786 --> 00:04:28.727
Like a program running in
the background silently.

00:04:28.727 --> 00:04:31.127
While we're busy doing other stuff."

00:04:31.127 --> 00:04:33.017
How many programs do you have saying

00:04:33.017 --> 00:04:36.084
I can't, I won't, I'm not good enough,

00:04:36.084 --> 00:04:38.740
I don't have enough money,
I'm not strong enough?

00:04:38.740 --> 00:04:40.403
And these things limit us.

00:04:40.403 --> 00:04:43.006
They're like a program running
in the back of our brain

00:04:43.006 --> 00:04:46.733
as if it's been hacked by
society and by life in general

00:04:46.733 --> 00:04:49.385
and by our experiences, trying to stop us

00:04:49.385 --> 00:04:51.197
from doing what we want to do.

00:04:51.197 --> 00:04:54.044
And I think a big point
that this show points out

00:04:54.044 --> 00:04:56.349
is that those background
processes, those thoughts

00:04:56.349 --> 00:04:58.052
that have been implanted in our brain,

00:04:58.052 --> 00:04:59.568
we don't have to listen to 'em.

00:04:59.568 --> 00:05:02.164
We can change the world
one step at a time.

00:05:02.164 --> 00:05:03.622
Do what we were born to do

00:05:03.622 --> 00:05:06.148
and be the entrepreneur
we've dreamed of being.

00:05:06.148 --> 00:05:08.925
Marcus from Affiliate
Marketing Dude, over and out.

00:05:08.925 --> 00:05:09.758
Back to you, Evan.

00:05:09.758 --> 00:05:12.341
(hip hop beat)

00:05:13.650 --> 00:05:15.067
Number five is Shark Tank,

00:05:15.067 --> 00:05:17.899
you guys probably are familiar
with it, a super hit TV show.

00:05:17.899 --> 00:05:19.752
And what I'm really grateful
for 'cause it helped put

00:05:19.752 --> 00:05:21.219
entrepreneurship on the map.

00:05:21.219 --> 00:05:23.862
It's fun to tune in and watch
some of the ideas that are

00:05:23.862 --> 00:05:26.053
pitched, sometimes they're
crazy and you laugh at them,

00:05:26.053 --> 00:05:28.308
sometimes you tune in just
to see the Sharks fighting

00:05:28.308 --> 00:05:30.419
with each other and
the drama that happens.

00:05:30.419 --> 00:05:32.130
But for me I really like to see

00:05:32.130 --> 00:05:35.408
how these successful
investors break down a deal,

00:05:35.408 --> 00:05:37.930
what they look for, how
they negotiate the deals,

00:05:37.930 --> 00:05:39.785
what the counters are
for the entrepreneurs,

00:05:39.785 --> 00:05:42.159
and seeing the pitches I
think is really good business

00:05:42.159 --> 00:05:45.174
education as well as providing
some entertainment value too.

00:05:45.174 --> 00:05:46.549
So if you haven't already seen it,

00:05:46.549 --> 00:05:48.366
I don't know what rock you're living under

00:05:48.366 --> 00:05:49.800
but it's definitely worth checking out.

00:05:49.800 --> 00:05:52.383
(hip hop beat)

00:05:53.588 --> 00:05:55.065
Number six is Suits.

00:05:55.065 --> 00:05:56.611
This is a fun show that's actually

00:05:56.611 --> 00:05:59.072
filmed here in Toronto, woo N-city!

00:05:59.072 --> 00:06:02.244
It's about a law firm, it's
about these Harvard Law

00:06:02.244 --> 00:06:05.595
students and one of the
lawyers, super successful,

00:06:05.595 --> 00:06:09.573
is the killer, always wins and
always has a ton of attitude

00:06:09.573 --> 00:06:13.993
and confidence and ego and
bravado and the new upstart guy

00:06:13.993 --> 00:06:15.812
doesn't have as much confidence but

00:06:15.812 --> 00:06:18.794
also has a lot of heart and caring

00:06:18.794 --> 00:06:20.470
and he wants to fight for the little guy

00:06:20.470 --> 00:06:23.027
and his boss doesn't
really see it all the time.

00:06:23.027 --> 00:06:25.590
There's a lot of fun
banter in between them

00:06:25.590 --> 00:06:28.064
and a lot of movie references
and pop culture references

00:06:28.064 --> 00:06:30.523
that you may understand or
may slide under the radar

00:06:30.523 --> 00:06:33.272
but it's a good show to kind
of, I like it because you see

00:06:33.272 --> 00:06:35.293
business people doing their thing,

00:06:35.293 --> 00:06:38.848
having confidence and bravado
and winning in their arena

00:06:38.848 --> 00:06:41.884
and so it's worth checking
out Season One at least.

00:06:41.884 --> 00:06:43.937
I loved Season One, it was amazing.

00:06:43.937 --> 00:06:46.919
As it got on, I think they're
in Season six or seven now,

00:06:46.919 --> 00:06:49.627
the in-between seasons felt
like they went a little too

00:06:49.627 --> 00:06:51.443
heavy on the drama for me,

00:06:51.443 --> 00:06:53.166
too much drama happening in each episode

00:06:53.166 --> 00:06:54.639
but then they kind of brought it back

00:06:54.639 --> 00:06:56.659
to this last season I'm
really enjoying again so

00:06:56.659 --> 00:06:58.733
watch Season One and see if you like it.

00:06:58.733 --> 00:07:00.657
If you do, it's worth continuing on.

00:07:00.657 --> 00:07:03.240
(hip hop beat)

00:07:04.425 --> 00:07:06.238
And number seven is Planet of the Apps.

00:07:06.238 --> 00:07:08.091
This is a yet to be released show.

00:07:08.091 --> 00:07:09.743
I heard about it from Gary Vanyerchuk.

00:07:09.743 --> 00:07:13.606
It's him, Gwyneth Paltrow,
will.i.am, and Jessica Alba

00:07:13.606 --> 00:07:16.064
and they are basically judging people

00:07:16.064 --> 00:07:17.790
who are pitching the apps so

00:07:17.790 --> 00:07:20.323
people have to go on
this escalator ride down

00:07:20.323 --> 00:07:21.896
and while they're on the
escalator they have to

00:07:21.896 --> 00:07:25.410
pitch their idea and one of
the four judges has to say

00:07:25.410 --> 00:07:28.346
I like you and then the
judges pick a winner

00:07:28.346 --> 00:07:30.519
and they personally work with that person

00:07:30.519 --> 00:07:31.706
to help them build their app

00:07:31.706 --> 00:07:35.105
and there's some competition
to see who ends up winning

00:07:35.105 --> 00:07:36.567
from all the apps and the coaching

00:07:36.567 --> 00:07:38.301
with the experts on there.

00:07:38.301 --> 00:07:40.101
So it hasn't come out,
I've only seen the trailer

00:07:40.101 --> 00:07:42.442
but there's some interesting people on it

00:07:42.442 --> 00:07:44.568
and I'm looking forward to
seeing the show come out

00:07:44.568 --> 00:07:46.232
and anything that's
supporting entrepreneurship

00:07:46.232 --> 00:07:48.259
generally I'm a pretty big fan of.

00:07:48.259 --> 00:07:49.633
So that's my take on the seven

00:07:49.633 --> 00:07:51.140
must-watch shows for entrepreneurs.

00:07:51.140 --> 00:07:53.205
I'd love to know, what did you guys think?

00:07:53.205 --> 00:07:54.890
Have you watched all seven of these?

00:07:54.890 --> 00:07:56.165
Do you have a favorite?

00:07:56.165 --> 00:07:57.400
Did I miss an eight, nine, 10

00:07:57.400 --> 00:07:58.753
that you want to add to the list?

00:07:58.753 --> 00:08:00.201
Leave it down in the comments below.

00:08:00.201 --> 00:08:01.499
I'm super curious to find out.

00:08:01.499 --> 00:08:03.460
I also want to give a quick
shout out to Kevin Fiedler

00:08:03.460 --> 00:08:06.306
from kevinfiedler.de,
thank you so much Kevin

00:08:06.306 --> 00:08:08.766
for picking up a copy of
my book, Your One Word

00:08:08.766 --> 00:08:11.064
and making the animated
review on it as well.

00:08:11.064 --> 00:08:12.639
I'm so glad you loved it

00:08:12.639 --> 00:08:14.218
and I really appreciate the support.

00:08:14.218 --> 00:08:16.716
So thank you guys again for
watching, I believe in you.

00:08:16.716 --> 00:08:18.859
I hope you continue to believe in yourself

00:08:18.859 --> 00:08:20.610
and whatever your one word is.

00:08:20.610 --> 00:08:22.785
Much love, I'll see ya soon.

00:08:22.785 --> 00:08:25.118
(swooshing)

